:"In the fields of computational linguistics and probability, an n-gram is a contiguous sequence of n items from a given sequence of text or speech. The items can be phonemes, syllables, letters, words or base pairs according to the application. The n-grams typically are collected from a text or speech corpus. When the items are words, n-grams may also be called shingles.[1]  An n-gram of size 1 is referred to as a \"unigram\"; size 2 is a \"bigram\" (or, less commonly, a \"digram\"); size 3 is a \"trigram\". Larger sizes are sometimes referred to by the value of n, e.g., \"four-gram\", \"five-gram\", and so on.","topics":[],"score":214052,"global_rank":253744,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":39985},{"name":"jamesbiederbeck/HashAppraiser","owner":"jamesbiederbeck","html_url":"https://github.com/jamesbiederbeck/HashAppraiser","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":214045,"global_rank":253763,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":39986},{"name":"crashtack/t_homework","owner":"crashtack","html_url":"https://github.com/crashtack/t_homework","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":214032,"global_rank":253806,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":39987},{"name":"pillai-ashwin/algodesc","owner":"pillai-ashwin","html_url":"https://github.com/pillai-ashwin/algodesc","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"A command line tool to display your code written in languages you code in for your reference.","topics":[],"score":214032,"global_rank":253811,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":39988},{"name":"gray-m/character-lstm-mal","owner":"gray-m","html_url":"https://github.com/gray-m/character-lstm-mal","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":214032,"global_rank":253817,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank